transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>The drive to the nearest hospital</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">From</th><th scope="col">Nearest hospital</th><th scope="col" class="n">Minutes by car</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/myrtle-trace/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Myrtle Trace</a></th><td data-label="Nearest hospital">Conway Medical Center</td><td class="n" data-label="Minutes by car">About 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Seasons at Prince Creek West</a></th><td data-label="Nearest hospital">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td class="n" data-label="Minutes by car">About 8</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-grande-dunes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Del Webb at Grande Dunes</a></th><td data-label="Nearest hospital">Grand Strand Medical Center</td><td class="n" data-label="Minutes by car">About 6</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach</a></th><td data-label="Nearest hospital">McLeod Health Seacoast</td><td class="n" data-label="Minutes by car">About 10; North Strand ER, 5</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">McLeod Health cut the ribbon on a new 48-bed hospital in Carolina Forest. Medicare's star ratings for every hospital here are on <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/care-compare/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Care Compare</a>. Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/healthcare/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">healthcare page</a> has more on care here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="hurricanes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Hurricanes and flooding">Do the 55+ communities have to evacuate for hurricanes?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three of the four are outside every hurricane evacuation zone. Every home in Seasons at Prince Creek West is in Zone C.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina divides the coast into <a href="https://www.scemd.org/prepare/know-your-zone/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">evacuation zones</a> A, B and C, drawn around storm surge, the rise of sea water in a storm. A home outside every zone is not ordered out by zone. The wind still reaches it.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Hurricane zone and flood cover</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Community</th><th scope="col">Hurricane evacuation zone</th><th scope="col" class="n">A flood policy nearby, a year</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/myrtle-trace/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Myrtle Trace</a></th><td data-label="Hurricane evacuation zone">Outside every zone</td><td class="n" data-label="A flood policy nearby, a year">About $550</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Seasons at Prince Creek West</a></th><td data-label="Hurricane evacuation zone">Zone C, every home</td><td class="n" data-label="A flood policy nearby, a year">About $600</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-grande-dunes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Del Webb at Grande Dunes</a></th><td data-label="Hurricane evacuation zone">Outside every zone</td><td class="n" data-label="A flood policy nearby, a year">About $550</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach</a></th><td data-label="Hurricane evacuation zone">Outside every zone</td><td class="n" data-label="A flood policy nearby, a year">About $600</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">All four communities are in FEMA's lower-risk flood zone. Federal law does not require flood insurance there, though a lender may still ask for it. In Seasons, 45 lots touch the high-risk zone at an edge. A lot's zone is not always the house's zone, so we check where the house is on the lot.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance guide</a> explains wind and flood cover, and our <a href="/buyers/relocating/hurricanes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">hurricane page</a> has more on storms here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="weather"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Weather">What is the weather like in Myrtle Beach all year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inland Conway has more than twice as many hot summer days as the coast. January afternoons are in the upper 50s in both.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Weather in a normal year</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">In a normal year</th><th scope="col">Myrtle Beach, on the coast</th><th scope="col">Conway, inland</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>Days of 90 degrees or more</th><td data-label="Myrtle Beach, on the coast">About 22</td><td data-label="Conway, inland">About 58</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span>Nights at or below freezing</th><td data-label="Myrtle Beach, on the coast">38</td><td data-label="Conway, inland">About 40</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>A January afternoon</th><td data-label="Myrtle Beach, on the coast">About 56 degrees</td><td data-label="Conway, inland">About 58 degrees</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the off season, nothing closes except the tourist attractions and the water parks. The boardwalk stays open, sometimes with shorter hours. Winter feels more open, because there are fewer people.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/weather/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">weather page</a> has more.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="retiring-to-myrtle-beach-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Retiring to Myrtle Beach FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How do I apply for the homestead exemption in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Apply at the Horry County Auditor's office, and inside a city at the city too, by July 15 for that year's bill. You must own the home, live in it as your legal home, have lived in South Carolina for a year, and have turned 65 by December 31 of the year before. The exemption takes the first $50,000 of the home's value off the tax.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can grandchildren visit a 55+ community near Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, with limits that differ by community. In Del Webb at Grande Dunes, a visitor under 19 may stay overnight up to 90 days in any 12 months. In Seasons at Prince Creek West, a visitor under 18 may stay up to 60 days a year. In Myrtle Trace, no minimum age applies to anyone else in the home once one person is 55 or older.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What makes a community 55+ under federal law?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">To count as 55+ housing under federal fair housing law, a community needs at least one person 55 or older in at least 80 percent of its occupied homes. It must also publish and follow its age policy, and check ages.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many people 65 and older live in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3 in 10 people in Horry County are 65 or older, against about 2 in 10 in South Carolina and in the U.S. as a whole.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does South Carolina tax Social Security?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. South Carolina does not tax Social Security at all. Pensions and IRAs also get a deduction for each person, larger from the year you turn 65, and military retirement pay is deducted in full at any age.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess126_2025-2026/bills/4216.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Act 110</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/policies/IL26-20.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR letter 26-20</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c006.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-6</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">12-37</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess126_2025-2026/appropriations2026/tap1b.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Proviso 117.220</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 county levy</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/assessor/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County assessor</a>, <a href="https://www.scemd.org/media/2202/2026-annex-c-evacuation-zones-and-clearance-times.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC hurricane zones</a>, <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/care-compare/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Care Compare</a>, <a href="https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/land-based-station/us-climate-normals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA normals</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSST1Y2025.S0101?g=050XX00US45051" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/3607" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 U.S.C. 3607</a>. Not legal or tax advice. Tax examples worked out by Chapter3 under the 2026 rules. Full-time homes and hurricane zones: every home in the county's parcel records, tested by Chapter3. Drives without traffic.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Myrtle Trace from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/polic